  "body": "A new **Tormach PathPilot Lathe** post (`assets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps`). PathPilot is LinuxCNC, so Fanuc Lathe output doesn't run on a Tormach lathe (#612).\n\n## Sources (cited in the script header and `docs/decisions/612-pathpilot-lathe-post.md`)\n- [LinuxCNC G-code reference](https://linuxcnc.org/docs/html/gcode/g-code.html) and [Lathe User Information](https://linuxcnc.org/docs/html/lathe/lathe-user.html): under G7, X is a diameter but the arc's I stays a radius.\n- Tormach's public 15L and 8L programming pages: the T word is tool + geometry offset; no M6; G7 only; G18 only; G20/G21 before motion; G76 I/J/K are diameter values; G30 before tool changes; no G80/G81/G83/G43.\n\n## How each operation posts\n- **Header:** `G7 G18 G20|G21 G90 G91.1 G40 G95`, then `G64 P…`. No `%` and no O word, since LinuxCNC's O is a subroutine label.\n- **Tool change:** `G30`, then `T0101` (tool 1-99).\n- **Spindle:** `G97 S.. M3`, or `G96 D<machine max rpm> S<surface speed> M3`.\n- **Facing, turning, profiling, grooving:** X is a diameter, feeds are G95 per revolution, arcs are `G2/G3 X Z I K`.\n- **Threading:** `G33 Z.. K<lead>`, with one G33 per pass (half-turns merged so the spindle-index sync starts once per pass); no G32. Optionally a one-block **`G76 P Z I J R K Q H`** cycle, chosen with the threading picker on the Post page.\n- **Drilling on centre:** plain G0/G1 on X0, plus `G4 P<s>` for a floor dwell. PathPilot's lathe has no drilling cycles.\n- **After each op and at the end:** `M1`/`M0`/`G30`; the program ends `M9 M5 G30 M30`.\n- **Refused by name:**\n  - tapping, back-boring, holes off the axis;\n  - G76 records the cycle can't state exactly (compound angle, finish allowance, pull-out, unequal rungs, internal thread, or one cut from −X);\n  - tool numbers outside 1-99;\n  - nose-radius compensation;\n  - milling work;\n  - feeds with no speed;\n  - C-axis sections.\n- **Registration:** added to `BUILTINS` and `LATHE_POSTS`. The default lathe post is still Fanuc Lathe.\n- **Not handled yet:** the threading stack's infeed and repeat-pass features (#516-#518) aren't on main. Each will need its own mapping or refusal when it lands.\n\n## How tested\n- **New `lathe_post_tormach` (9):**\n  - goldens for turning, G33 threading, G76 threading and an axial drill, each in mm and inch, run through both the in-app gate and the raw stream;\n  - a dwell;\n  - G96 with D;\n  - an arc;\n  - part load;\n  - a trip home;\n  - the dialect refusals and the G76 refusals;\n  - the registry.\n- **LinuxCNC syntax check on every program:** G7 before motion, no nested comments, only documented G/M words, and no G32, G80, G81, G83, M6, G43, Y, O or `%`.\n- **Conformance:** it now requires the new post to refuse every mill golden by name.\n- **Gate:** golden_cl, posting, every lathe_post* and turning_* suite, machine_library, after_op, the coolant suites, tormach_post and camcraft-post all pass. Clippy is clean.\n\n## Not exercised (draft until the Hub run)\n- **Hub run:** a turning and a threading program in PathPilot Hub's 8L or 15L simulator (the issue's Done means). The machines are #611 / PR #624.\n- **Assumptions to confirm on the control:**\n  - G30 before each tool change (no G53 retract);\n  - I/K arcs;\n  - one G33 per pass;\n  - the G76 I sign for tools touched off at +X.\n\nChangelog: New Tormach PathPilot Lathe post (LinuxCNC G7/G18/G95, T0101, G33 passes or one-block G76 threading, drilling on centre as plain moves); selectable for lathes, with refusals by name for what PathPilot cannot run (#612)\n\nRefs #612\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
